[- Reference: Tables, streaming, ast-bin, data-bin. -]
[page id='tables'
  [meta
    title='Tables, Streaming, and Binary Formats'
    layout='reference'
    nav-order='440'
    audience='user'
    summary='Tabular data, event-driven IO, and the binary forms underneath.'
  ]

  [section id='tables' title='The Table API'
    [prose A CX table is a structural form for columnar data. Columns declare a name and a type; rows are records. The Table API exposes count, schema introspection, dump, and load — symmetric inverses with declared types preserved across formats.]
    [code lang='cx' src='''[:table
  [:col name='size'  type='string']
  [:col name='count' type='int']
  [:row [size 'large'] [count 12]]
  [:row [size 'small'] [count 8]]]''']
    [code lang='shell' src='''cx table info orders.cx     # column / row counts, types, byte size
cx table dump orders.cx --to=cx
cx table load orders.csv --to=cx''']
  ]

  [section id='streaming' title='Streaming Parse and Emit'
    [prose Streaming parse and emit move bytes through the runtime without ever holding the whole tree in memory. Callbacks fire per element-start, attribute, body chunk, and element-end. The same callback shape works on every input format.]
    [code lang='python' src='''with open('events.cx', 'rb') as f:
    for event in cx.stream(f):
        if event.kind == 'element_start' and event.name == 'error':
            print(event.attrs)''']
    [prose Use streaming when the input is large enough that resident memory matters — log files, telemetry dumps, large XML / JSON / CXDB sources. The tree API materialises everything; streaming materialises nothing.]
  ]

  [section id='write' title='Streaming Emit'
    [code lang='python' src='''with cx.stream_writer(open('out.cx', 'wb')) as w:
    for record in fetch_records():
        w.write(record)''']
    [prose RSS stays bounded regardless of the output size. Tier-1 bindings (V, Python, Go) ship the streaming writer; Tier-2/3 follow in the v0.7.x window.]
  ]

  [section id='ast-bin' title='ast-bin: Binary AST'
    [prose ast-bin is a binary serialization of the CXDM tree designed for fast cross-binding handoff and stable disk storage. Compact, versioned, and round-trip-byte-identical with the text form. Used for the FFI boundary in every binding and for canonical-bytes comparisons in the conformance suite. Capability bit 29 advertises v6; bindings query cx_features before reading a payload.]
  ]

  [section id='data-bin' title='data-bin: Arrow and Parquet'
    [prose data-bin connects the CX Table API to the columnar formats the analytics ecosystem already speaks — Apache Arrow for in-process exchange, Parquet for on-disk storage. The bridges live in libcx_arrow; the CX side stays format-agnostic. Phase A (Arrow round-trip) ships in v0.7.0; Phase B (Parquet writer) and Phase C (read-side schema inference) follow.]
    [code lang='shell' src='''cx table dump orders.cx --to=parquet > orders.parquet
cx table load orders.parquet --to=cx''']
  ]

